WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:28.790
Joe Biden's wife, Jill Biden, potentially
the future first lady of the United States,

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:32.210
depending on what happens in November, is
pretty clever.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:35.160
And she's also quite astute when it comes
to dealing with media.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.160
Now, certainly she's had media training.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:42.180
I'm guessing it has been ramped up, given
that Joe Biden is the nominee up, but she

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.990
seems to have a bit of a natural ability for
this.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:49.399
I'm going to play a clip for you today of
Jill Biden completely shutting down CNN's

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:53.829
Jake Tapper, who tries to bring up the issue
of Joe Biden's gaffe.

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:58.710
And Jill, Biden does something that is really
it's a clinic on how to be interviewed.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.100
She says gaffes.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.320
Trump is president.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.490
What are you talking about?

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:04.949
Joe Biden's gaffe.

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:07.310
So I'm going to play the clip for you.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.580
Then we'll discuss it.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.380
I'm resisting my instinct to first tell you
all of the interesting things about this clip.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.720
I'm not going to do that.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.510
Let's watch it first and then we will talk
about it.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.470
Your husband has been known to make the occasional
gaffe.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.549
You can't even go there.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:27.380
You can after Donald Trump.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.380
You know, I wanted to say the word.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.170
I can't say the word gaffe now, but, you know,
done.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.780
It's gone.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.400
The gaffe issue is over.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.400
So over.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.920
So Jake Tapper doesn't even know how to respond.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:47.210
And what Jill Biden did here is super interesting,
both from the perspective of the interviewer

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.280
and the perspective of the interviewee.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.990
Now, I've been on both sides of this.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:56.280
I've been the interviewer asking questions
of a guest that the guests may not want to

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.280
answer.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:02.869
I've also been a guest being asked questions
that either, you know, it's not typically

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:06.270
that I don't want to answer them, but that
I either find boring or lame or distracting

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.469
or improperly framed questions.

00:02:08.469 --> 00:02:10.219
So I've been on both sides of this.

00:02:10.219 --> 00:02:16.069
Jill Biden has handled this perfectly in that
she resisted opening up the can of worms.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:21.010
She reframed as we talk about it in a moment,
you'll see what I mean.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:27.319
And she did it in a charming and friendly
way without attacking the interviewer and

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:32.549
without making it awkward, but simultaneously
reminding the audience of how absurd it is

00:02:32.549 --> 00:02:37.000
to talk about Joe Biden's gaffes when the
president is Donald Trump.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.689
There are two other ways that she could have
done this.

00:02:39.689 --> 00:02:42.530
Based on the typical media training and preparation.

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:46.129
So one thing that Jill Biden could have done,
and she didn't do it.

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:50.189
One thing she could have done is to do a typical
standard reframe and pivot.

00:02:50.189 --> 00:02:56.760
Okay, so that would be something like acknowledging
Biden's gaffes, but pivoting to issues which

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.839
would start with some kind of mild acknowledgment.

00:02:58.839 --> 00:03:02.199
It might be, you know, what about what about
the gaffes?

00:03:02.199 --> 00:03:05.339
You know, my husband, he says what's on his
mind, he's passionate.

00:03:05.339 --> 00:03:10.420
And sometimes things come out in a way that
he would redo if given the chance.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.750
But what this election is really about is
the future of this country and health care

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.019
and coronavirus.

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:20.079
So I'm sure if you've watched any interviews
in your life, you've heard people respond

00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:21.730
that way when interviewed.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:26.120
And the downside of it is it does feel like
not answering the question because it's not

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.529
really answering the question.

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:29.829
So she didn't do that the other way.

00:03:29.829 --> 00:03:34.730
Joe Biden could have responded, would have
been to sort of more forcefully and noticeably

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.150
refused to answer.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.769
And that often looks very bad.

00:03:37.769 --> 00:03:38.769
Right.

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:40.400
So I'm not here to talk about that.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.849
Or this is an election about issues, not about
gaffes or no comment.

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:45.849
Right.

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:47.260
I mean, that's really, really bad.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.260
That's not good.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.349
And she didn't do that.

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:53.260
But what Jill Biden does and we're going to
watch it a second time now, armed with the

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:57.370
knowledge of how to interpret this, what Jill
Biden does is to essentially make it a big

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:03.870
joke while being friendly and reminding people
that Biden's gaffes are nothing compared to

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:10.819
Trump's years of insults and attacks, attacks
and mocking of disabled reporter using racist

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:16.230
and xenophobic terms, suggesting people inject
bleach and on and on and on and the way, you

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.049
know that this was effective.

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:19.049
Is that Jeff?

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:20.590
Jake Tapper.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:21.870
He's just out of ideas.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.919
He retreats to just repeating what she says.

00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:28.360
Jake Tapper says, oh, the issue is over.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.360
Let's look at it.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:36.940
One more time, your husband has been known
to make the occasional gaffe, you can't even

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:37.940
go there.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:41.610
You can after Donald Trump, you get what I
want and say the word.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.320
I can't even say the word gaffe now.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.400
But, you know, done.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.990
It's gone.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.169
The gaffe issue is over.

00:04:48.169 --> 00:04:49.680
We are so over.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.520
So this might not seem that notable if you
don't look at it more deeply, but that is

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:59.860
actually a very skilled and tactful way to
handle this question and this issue.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.180
And by the way, it's not just optics.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.280
Jill Biden is right.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.280
Sure.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.430
Joe Biden has been gaffe prone over the years.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:13.380
Donald Trump gaffes every week of this presidency
as much as Joe Biden has in the last decade.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:17.710
And she was able to make that point without
insulting Jake Tapper, without attacking the

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.520
question or the network.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.169
It's also, quite frankly, a bit of a lazy
question.

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:25.440
Let let's now look at it from the interviewer's
point of view.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:31.629
If Jake Tapper wants to prevent Jill Biden
from being able to do this, he has to come

00:05:31.629 --> 00:05:33.449
up with something more specific.

00:05:33.449 --> 00:05:38.550
Your husband once said X and that was deeply
offensive to Y.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.410
Why do you think he hasn't apologized?

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:43.219
Is he unwilling to admit that that was a mistake?

00:05:43.219 --> 00:05:49.280
You have to frame the question more powerfully,
because if Jake Tapper does that, Jill Biden

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.569
can't get out of it as easily and as smoothly
as she did.

00:05:52.569 --> 00:05:56.990
So this is partially that Jill Biden handled
the question really well and wasn't going

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:01.750
to put up with this absurd idea that the Biden
gaffes are the problem when you look at the

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.599
last four years of Trump.

00:06:03.599 --> 00:06:08.470
But also, Jake Tapper brought it up in sort
of a lazy way and it allowed her to do this.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:15.460
But her identifying it quickly and diffusing
it in a friendly and cordial way was what

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.660
was astute, really, a clinic on how to handle
interviews.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.020
Let me know what you think.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:24.930
Let me know what you're expecting for tonight's
debate, which we will be live for starting

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:28.289
at eight thirty p.m. Eastern Time on YouTube,
Twitch and Facebook.

00:06:28.289 --> 00:06:30.550
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:31.969
I look forward to hearing from you.

